  "content_id": "16135990",
  "title": "Install Edge on your Macbook",
  "description": "Edge - Crypto &amp; Bitcoin Wallet can also be downloaded from the Apple App Store onto your MacBook or iMac with any M-series chip if you...",
  "body": "<p class=\"no-margin\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/edge-crypto-bitcoin-wallet/id1344400091\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"intercom-content-link\">Edge - Crypto &amp; Bitcoin Wallet</a> can also be downloaded from the Apple App Store onto your MacBook or iMac with any M-series chip if you want to run the app from your desktop. Edge is primarily focused on creating the best mobile experience, and all of our cutting-edge security protocols, such as biometric authentication and a robust <a href=\"https://support.edge.app/hc/en-us/articles/7018106439579\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"intercom-content-link\">IP Validation and 2FA</a> account system, will still function perfectly from your personal Mac.</p><p class=\"no-margin\"><i>Operating Edge from a Chromebook or from a mobile phone emulator program on a Windows PC will also work; however, the app may not perform as quickly, and biometric sign-in will be unavailable. </i></p><p class=\"no-margin\"><i>WalletConnect is also available to you within Edge on your mobile device. This would allow you to interact with decentralized apps (dApps) on another device, such as a computer, while securely authorizing or signing transactions from your smartphone.</i></p>",
  "author_id": 9849332,
